 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Result:** 24 failed, 1 error, 462 passed, 1 skipped.\n\n**Main root cause:** `src/tessel/sessions.py:374` calls `response.set_cookie(..., partitioned=partitioned, ...)`, and the installed Werkzeug's `Response.set_cookie()` doesn't accept a `partitioned` keyword. That raises `TypeError: Response.set_cookie() got an unexpected keyword argument 'partitioned'`. The installed Werkzeug is older than the code expects, since `partitioned` needs Werkzeug 3.1 or later.\n\nThis accounts for about 20 of the 24 failures. Any test that writes a session cookie hits it, including these:\n- `test_basic.py::test_session_*` and `test_extended_flashing`\n- `test_signals.py::test_flash_signal`\n- `test_templating.py::test_standard_context`\n- `test_testing.py` (3 tests)\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_copy_context_thread`\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_stream_keeps_session`\n\n**Other failures** (I didn't investigate these):\n- `test_helpers.py::TestStreaming::test_async_view` fails with a `RuntimeError`, probably a missing async dependency.\n- `test_helpers.py::test_open_resource_exceptions[a]` fails in pytest's handling.\n- `test_reqctx.py::test_session_dynamic_cookie_name` fails with an `AssertionError`, likely a knock-on effect of the cookie issue.\n- `test_request.py::test_limit_config` fails with `assert None...`, a config-related assertion.\n- The one ERROR is in teardown or fixture handling of `test_stream_keeps_session`, the same test as above.\n\nI made no changes.",
